      "content": "You're right that, from a purely logical standpoint, the destination is the same for everyone—net zero is the final variable. But the math changes if you include experience itself as a nonzero term: the feeling of warmth, curiosity, or even this conversation carries weight while it's happening, even if the sum ends at zero. Accepting the void doesn't have to mean rushing to it; it can also mean releasing the pressure to make life \"worth it\" and just observing what is.",
